Space Capacity is part of Data Center Control Plane (DCCP), Tranche 2: Facility
Capacity and Placement. It is repository 11 of the canonical 72-runtime DCCP and
owns physical-space capacity accounting across facility containment: stable
location identities and generations, the containment hierarchy, spatial class,
rack and rack-unit envelopes, occupancy claims, reserved footprint, expansion
zones, incompatibility and exclusion regions, and service-clearance constraints,
in exact integer units.

It consumes identities and hierarchy from Physical Location Registry, Facility
Topology, Rack Registry, Asset Registry and policy references, and it owns none
of them. It does not own power, cooling, aggregate facility capacity, placement
planning or future reservation authority, and it never grants placement.

Third-party notices
-------------------

This product includes no third-party source code and links no third-party
libraries. It is implemented against the C++20 standard library and the
operating-system interfaces it needs for durable atomic file replacement and
advisory file locking.

The canonical serialization format, the integrity digest (SHA-256, FIPS 180-4),
the CRC-32 header check value, and every identity, generation and epoch type are
implemented in this repository.

Space Capacity does not collect or transmit any telemetry. It opens no network
sockets, performs no name resolution, and contacts no remote service. All state
it writes is written to local files chosen by the operator and never leaves the
machine running the software.

